  "decision_conditions": [
    "The Council does not consider that the grounds specified by the applicant/agent sufficient reason to justify the proposed excessive and premature crown reduction of a mature and prominent tree of significant amenity that makes a positive contribution to the amenity of the locality and wider borough.",
    "The proposed works conflict with the recommendations in BS3998:2010, by removing too much leaf bearing structure \"there should still be a strong framework of healthy small diameter and twigs (leaf bearing structure) capable of producing dense leaf cover during the following growing season\", and by inflicting unreasonable wounds on the tree \"the cuts should not exceed 100mm in diameter\".",
    "The tree is still recovering from previous works, and the specified amount to be removed goes beyond previous reduction points and beyond sound arboricultural practice. A longer period of time is required before further crown works are carried out to the tree. It should be considered when making assessment as to any requirement of works, that the tree is growing older and decreasing in energy levels as a result of it's age and previous works."
  ],
